  {
   "evidence": "The definition sets `distribution x := LinearMap.ker (\u03c3.bilinFormAt x)`, so `\u03c3` determines the distribution but is not itself the distribution.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/TwoForm/Kernel.lean",
   "fix": "Reword: \"for a closed two-form `\u03c3` whose kernels all have dimension `k`, the `C^n` foliation of rank `k` whose tangent distribution is `x \u21a6 ker \u03c3_x` (requires `1 \u2264 n`).\"",
   "issue": "The docstring says the two-form `\u03c3` \"is the tangent distribution `x \u21a6 ker \u03c3_x`\" of a foliation. A form is not a distribution, so this misdescribes the object being defined.",
   "line": 229
  }
